Purpose: Network defaults without Google: no network-time queries, Google Public DNS DoH provider disabled, IPv6 reachability probe uses the RFC 3849 documentation address instead of 2001:4860:4860::8888, omnibox AIM eligibility (a www.google.com request) off, search-engine preconnect off (kPreconnectToSearch: a TLS connection to the default search engine at startup).
Area: debrand
Files: components/network_time/network_time_tracker.cc; net/dns/public/doh_provider_entry.cc; net/dns/host_resolver_manager.cc; components/omnibox/browser/aim_eligibility_service_features.cc; chrome/browser/navigation_predictor/search_engine_preconnector.cc
Rebase risk: low because five independent one-line edits in stable code. Geolocation contacts Google only when a site asks for it, so it is left alone (see M3-G2 report)
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)

